# TF_GLM_PROFILE=1 under --parallel > 1: the multi-stream engine's whole-chunk prompt fills (multi.py _fill) never armed
# the prefill profiler, so with PARALLEL above 1 (the recipe's default) the only report was the start-up warm-up chunk.
# Arm it around prefill_chunk as decode.prefill does and report once per prompt, on every rank (so ranks can be
# compared). Sliced fills (while others decode) and grouped fills stay unprofiled. Tested on v1.5 at three Sparks:
# 19 reports per rank per benchmark run; off (the default) changes nothing.

diff --git tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/multi.py tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/multi.py
--- tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/multi.py
+++ tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/multi.py
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@
